      "observed": "The netlist includes both an ATtiny13V (U1) and an ATtiny45 (U4), with their supply pins and corresponding GPIO pins connected to the same nets. For example, both PB1 pins are on NET0008, and both VCC pins are on +5V.",
      "expected": "A single ATtiny should control the board, or the design should provide explicit selection or isolation if these are alternative MCU options. Two active MCUs sharing GPIO nets can contend when their outputs differ.",
