        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"PB3\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"XTAL1/PB3\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both listed MCUs are populated, their shared GPIOs may be driven to conflicting levels, causing incorrect fan-control behavior or electrical stress. The netlist shows no selection or isolation between them.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design lists two powered ATtiny devices whose corresponding GPIOs are tied together, with no selection or isolation shown. This creates a credible output-contention risk unless assembly deliberately omits one device."
}

